# Deployment view

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
The deployment view describes the technical infrastructure and how the building blocks are mapped onto it: environments, data centers, nodes and networks.
{% /callout %}

## Infrastructure

| Node | Contents | Configuration |
|:---|:---|:---|
| AKS cluster "prod-weu" | All {% $system %} services | 3 nodes, zone-redundant |
| Azure Database for PostgreSQL | Data per service (separate schemas) | High availability, 35-day backups |
| Event Hubs (Kafka API) | Events between services | 4 partitions per topic |
| App stores | Mobile app | Distributed via MDM |

## Environments

| Environment | Purpose | Data |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Development | Integration of every change | Synthetic |
| Staging | Acceptance testing with dispatch | Anonymized copy |
| Production | Live operation | Real |
